Loop device allows a regular file to be treated as a block device
used by linux to build OS images, used by snap and disk image tools, can be used to create virtual disks (like sd card/flash), test filesystem

5.a to create loop device: losetup -f --partscan --show sd.img

5.b to show all loop devices in use: lsblk

5.c to detach: losetup -d /dev/loopx

